{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1498220-3e-essence-xianxia-campaign-rules-and-setting","id":1498220,"title":"[3e] [Essence] Xianxia Campaign Rules and Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-28T12:38:22-08:00","id":1498220,"title":"[3e] [Essence] Xianxia Campaign Rules and Setting","content":"After reading through my copy of Exalted Essence, I had a notion for a Xianxia game using Exalted. I couldn't really put the 3e version together until I had Exigents, but after getting a copy of that I was able to extend the idea there.<br /> <br /> For those who don't know, Xianxia is a genre of Chinese literature and media that focuses on the exploits of people and monsters who cultivate qi within themselves, growing in various stages of power. It is very clearly a major influence on Exalted, so I thought I'd reverse the flow and create some rules for running it. You will need a copy of Exalted Essence or Exalted 3e (and the Exigents book, optimally) in order to play it. Essence has the advantage of Universal Charms that make things a lot easier, while in 3e Cultivators will primarily be using modified Solar Charms (which, to be fair, were the basis of most Universal Charms anyway.)<br /> <br /> Cultivators get to be powerful - <b>very </b>powerful - and so they are presented here as Solar-tier Exigents, more or less. While you are very strong, it's worth noting that it's also a staple of the genre that monsters and spirits are <i>also</i> cultivators, so you'll have some pretty stiff opposition!<br /> <br /> I've also included an optional setting guide called Ladders of Heaven (though I was strongly tempted to call it &quot;Reach Heaven Through Violence&quot;. Those who have read Kill Six Billion Demons will know that one.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jq7gSFc5hm-HAtMNPgnc8FtvA47sEG4HC1jth8W_GTY\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e version</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BnUbiH5CWWxEPQtUo_dPSmgPJTjLzlhUHHongrZ22oI\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Essence version</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxKWn1Qj3-dX0MhHhtzj-vKFLLpfOLNG95ffXJJ4-SM\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Essence sheet</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iX17sJXnlMxsBs7ouLtCLsO0O37nCP6BfmA0oGWh1i8\" target=\"_blank\">Ladders of Heaven setting</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}